// Decoy: a copy of your ship that draws fire (projectiles hit it; seekers home on it).
// Integrity equals your max hull; it drifts along your
// aim at `launch_speed` for `duration_secs`, then snaps back to you like a rubber band at
// `return_speed` and hits the first ship on its path (teammates and you included, no
// friendly-fire scaling) for `return_fraction` (99%) of its remaining integrity, with
// `return_knockback_per_damage` u/s of push per point. A return that reaches nobody within
// `return_max_secs` fizzles. Press G to launch.
// Behaviour: crates/ls-sim/src/gadgets/decoy.rs. Schema: `ls_sim::GadgetDef`.
GadgetDef(
    id: "decoy",
    name: "Decoy",
    activation: Instant,
    energy_cost: 30.0,
    cooldown_secs: 10.0,
    duration_secs: 6.0,
    visual: (shape: Decoy, color: (255, 255, 255), scale: 1.0),
    params: {
        "return_fraction": 0.99,
        "return_speed": 60.0,
        "return_max_secs": 3.0,
        "return_knockback_per_damage": 0.2,
        "launch_speed": 12.0,
    },
)
